## Item 1 — MUST FIX (driver.cljc:943): post-cycle drain run-end re-labelled

**Fix** — the cond after the post-cycle drain now opens with the pre-cycle guard's mirror (`src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:944-949`): `(= :releasing (:phase base))` → `base`, placed *before* the `(some? end)` arm so a drain-ended run is never re-ended even when the cycle also queued a `:run-end`.

**Reachability test** — `delayed-carriage-past-the-bound-ends-the-run-once-test` (driver_test.cljc:1034). The machine halts (`:safepoint`), a real renewal is sent at `{:s 11}` and carried by the real front; the critical step withholds the carriage reply from the pre-cycle drain (a wrapper answering nil once, then the reply) and releases it inside the post-cycle drain, flipping a controlled-reading clock to the bound (`{:s 31}` = basis 1 + 30) at exactly that release — between-step clock resets provably cannot fire the arm.

**Red before the fix** — exactly the gate's four symptoms: phase `:releasing`→`:safepoint`, status `:yin.k/ended`→`:yin.k/ok`, ended detail lost (`:cause nil`), and a **second** run-end diagnostic on the next step (2 diagnostics, violating r3 1.6). **Green after**: one diagnostic, one release, the retry is the identical request.

## Item 2 — MUST PIN (driver.cljc:478-481): refusal → fresh pid

`two-candidates-over-two-encodings-test` extended: guards that the judge's granting pass really recorded `:dao.lease/rejected` for holder-b's pid in the ledger, lapses the winner's lease, steps holder-b again — fresh pid proposed, 2 distinct proposal ids total, `:proposals` 2. Pinned green (the discipline already held).

## Item 3 — RECOMMENDED (driver.cljc:924-926, :556-557): the epoch dimension

New `the-epoch-dimension-of-the-tenure-recheck-test` with a `crafted-ledger` helper: the world's own header/enrollment/offers plus a hand-built prior tenure (grant→lapse→reclaim) so the *same* grant fact is the occurrence's live lease **bound one epoch higher** — crafted directly because no foldable history can move an epoch under an unchanged lease id. The running recheck refuses `:stale` with `:dao.lease/observed-lease = l` (the epoch alone moved); accept's stale arm likewise refuses `not-holder` carrying the moved epoch, holder and lease of the successor tenure.

One honest boundary: accept's epoch disjunct cannot be *isolated* on foldable records — a reclaim (the only epoch mover) always nils the live lease first, so at accept a differing epoch entails a differing lease. The pin therefore drives the reachable stale path with the epoch dimension engaged and asserted (binding 1 vs observed 2), while the recheck half isolates the epoch alone through the evidence-captured-at-accept asymmetry. Both green with no code change.

